# process — OS/process infrastructure

`ProcessManager` is the public façade for start/stop/alive. Launch details stay in package-private helpers.

| Class | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| ProcessManager | Start/stop; `onExit` callback when the OS process dies |
| ProcessCommandBuilder | Shell wrap, JS/PHP port injection |
| ProcessLaunchEnv | PATH, JAVA_HOME, Maven/Node/PHP, UTF-8 |
| ProcessStartupPort | Detected/custom port, env, protected ports |
| ProcessRuntimeKind | JAVA / PHP / JS |
| ProcessOs | Windows check, PATH prepend |
| ProcessTreeKiller / PortProcessKiller | Tree kill and port free |
| ListeningPortScanner / DevPortHeuristics / ProcessSnapshot | LISTEN inventory |
| JavaVersionDetector / PhpVersionDetector | Runtime discovery |
| MavenLaunchCommands / WindowsCommandResolver | Launch command shape |
